<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 17.23 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 17.23 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to 17.23 percent at an auction on Tuesday from 18.02 percent at the last auction on May 7, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   May 13	     May 7</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K1408972     KZ43K0708976</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	  550		  600</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, million tenge)	 2,220		2,220</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	 601		  600</p>
<p> Average price			 95.87 pct	  95.69</p>
<p> Average yield			 17.23		18.02</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Aug 14, 1997     Aug 7, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
